  "headword": "{降機|こうき}",
  "reading": "こうき",
  "romaji": "kouki",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "disembarking (from an aircraft); deplaning",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "disembarking from an aircraft; getting off a plane",
      "explanation": "The act of leaving an aircraft after it lands. A formal term used mainly in aviation and airport announcements, the opposite of {搭乗|とうじょう} (boarding)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29366_kouki_ex1",
      "japanese": "{降機|こうき}の{準備|じゅんび}をする。",
      "english": "Prepare to disembark.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29366_kouki_ex2",
      "japanese": "{後方|こうほう}の{座席|ざせき}から{順|じゅん}に{降機|こうき}してください。",
      "english": "Please disembark in order, starting from the rear seats.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29366_kouki_ex3",
      "japanese": "{乗|の}り{継|つ}ぎの{乗客|じょうきゃく}は、{降機|こうき}{後|ご}に{係員|かかりいん}の{案内|あんない}に{従|したが}ってください。",
      "english": "Transferring passengers, please follow the staff's directions after disembarking.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A formal, written-style term heard mainly in airline and airport announcements. In everyday speech people usually say {飛行機|ひこうき}を{降|お}りる instead.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {降機|こうき}する: to disembark\n- {降機|こうき}{口|ぐち}: aircraft exit door\n- {降機|こうき}{時|じ}: at the time of disembarking\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {搭乗|とうじょう}: boarding — the opposite act of getting on an aircraft.\n- {下車|げしゃ}: getting off — used for trains and buses rather than planes.",
